  "details": "<p>This place is not to be confused with other similar or nearly identical toponyms. It is distinct from the <a class=\"internal-link\" href=\"resolveuid/1b7c05b4c4dc4173b4ceacec9be9fac8\" target=\"_self\" title=\"\">Timna Valley</a>, a site of copper mining, located near Eilat, Israel. <span>It is also distinct from\u00a0</span><a class=\"internal-link\" href=\"resolveuid/3c1e3faf6168154c19815130899f8e96\" target=\"_self\" title=\"\">Qasr Timnah</a>\u00a0located near the same valley<span>.\u00a0</span>It is also distinct from the place <a class=\"internal-link\" href=\"resolveuid/5d531a9f1dce463a14236f6a2488f5ff\" target=\"_self\" title=\"\">Tamna</a> in Yemen.\u00a0</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Tel Batash, an archaeological site located in the Sorek Valley of modern Israel, lies northwest of Beit Shemesh. This site has been identified as the ancient Timnath or Timnah, a Philistine city in Canaan.",
